# oracle: pair_style pace with a three-element .yace basis (the coupling_coefficients.yace of the LAMMPS example PACKAGES/pace/compute: H, N, O, FinnisSinclair, ChebExpCos per element pair) on that example's 161-atom cell (latte_cell_0.data), run 0 then 10 NVE steps
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE; see w257pace_recursive)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.7e-14, atoms 4.2e-14.
# oracle-examples: PACKAGES/pace/compute/latte_cell_0.data PACKAGES/pace/compute/coupling_coefficients.yace
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
atom_modify     map hash
read_data       latte_cell_0.data
mass            1 1.00
mass            2 14.00
mass            3 15.999
pair_style      pace
pair_coeff      * * coupling_coefficients.yace H N O
thermo_style    custom step pe press pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
velocity        all create 300 4928459 loop geom
fix             1 all nve
timestep        0.0002
thermo          5
run             10
